{
  "_": [
    "The option schema for the YouK range: what a customer is offered, and which",
    "part is behind each option. Read by src/engine/guided.js, which contains no",
    "part numbers of its own - this file is the whole of what makes that engine",
    "know about YouK, and the next range gets its own copy.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED, NOT DERIVED, and that is a decision rather than laziness. A",
    "taxonomy inferred from the supplier's filenames would be wrong about roughly",
    "one part in ten: 008533 is described as a 1200 mm part and measures 643.5 mm,",
    "008534 is called a rail in both languages and is the 900 mm extension, and",
    "008535's CAD is missing its bracket entirely. See youk/FINDINGS.md.",
    "",
    "TWO DIMENSIONS. Depth is the variant - it decides which frames exist and",
    "which depth-matched accessories do. Width is the size within it - it decides",
    "the span and the width-matched accessories. Both are real incompatibilities:",
    "a 320 mm frame will not take a 200 mm hook strip, and a 900 mm bay will not",
    "take a 1200 mm shoe rack.",
    "",
    "The 200 mm range's span is a TIMBER shelf. That is not a preference: there",
    "is no metal shelf for 200 mm depth anywhere in the 80 parts. Nothing derived",
    "from the names would have found that.",
    "",
    "Every componentId here is verified against what actually loaded, and a",
    "missing one refuses the build BY NAME rather than quietly shrinking the",
    "product - the same rule resolveConfiguration follows.",
    "",
    "`perBay: true` means the max is per bay rather than per product: one shoe",
    "rack per bay is a sensible ceiling, one per product is not, and the",
    "difference only shows up when somebody asks for three bays.",
    "",
    "NO SHOE RACKS (008553-008556), and that is not an omission. They carry no",
    "snaps at all, because youk/snap-spec.json _notThisSystem already records",
    "what MA 406213 says: they screw straight to a wall with plugs and screws,",
    "and no ladder appears in the sheet. Offering them here as bay accessories",
    "was an authoring mistake, and the engine caught it by answering \"there is",
    "nowhere on this product for that part\" - which was the truth. They belong",
    "in a guided flow as WALL-FIXED items, placed as a second anchor the way",
    "attach.js placeFree already handles, and that is not built yet.",
    "",
    "`spans: true` means the part bridges two frames and must be held at both",
    "ends. Without it a fourth shelf asked for in a bay with three free rungs",
    "was cantilevered off the outside of the run rather than refused.",
    "A3, 12 November 2026 (docs/audit/A1-failures.md): the 200 mm range defaults to the FLOOR and offers floor or wall only - its ladders have no fixing for a foot (F04); the 900 mm clothes rail and full-width hook strip are no longer listed for 200 mm deep, because both are 320 mm parts that can never attach there (F13); and a clothes rail is one PER BAY, so a three-bay wardrobe can have three (F12, Matt).",
    "B, 12 November 2026: every add names its `group` - \"storage\" (shelves, YouboXx) or \"accessories\" (rails, hook strips, side racks) - which is the step of the guided flow it appears in (direction C). The runtime reads it; nothing in code lists the kinds.",
    "Kits, 13 November 2026: cabinets (three heights) and desks (600/700 deep) are adds whose `kit` names a variant-level recipe in `kits` - the brackets, arms and clamps that carry them are placed with them and listed on the bill of materials. One kit per bay. Matt: all three heights, the cabinet on the bottom rung with the bay shelf moving up, the shared bracket chosen automatically, desks at the same time."
  ],
